 "description": "Deactivate one workflow's future production triggers without deleting saved data or stopping runs already in progress. workflowId must be the current stable ID from n8n_workflows_list or get, not a name or version ID. Use n8n_workflows_activate to reverse the state or archive for lifecycle removal. Requires unsafe mode plus deactivation permission; returns target-validated inactive state metadata.",
